<BaseLayout title="About" description="Who writes ObservedState and what this site is for.">
  <div class="container section">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>About ObservedState</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lede">
        ObservedState is a working notebook on ServiceNow ITOM and the CMDB, and on everything that connects to them:
        cloud, infrastructure as code, monitoring, data integration, and increasingly AI.
      </p>

      <h2>Who</h2>
      <p>
        I'm {SITE.author}, a ServiceNow Certified Technical Architect with 16 years of ServiceNow consulting and around
        30 in IT overall. [Add two or three sentences in your own words.]
      </p>

      <h2>Why "observed state"</h2>
      <p>
        Infrastructure has a declared state (what the template, the change record or the architecture diagram says) and
        an observed state (what is actually running). The gap between them is drift, and closing it is reconciliation.
        The CMDB is where that reconciliation shows up, which is why it sits at the center of this site.
      </p>

      <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/writing/">Writing</a>: field notes, deep dives and teardowns.</li>
        <li><a href="/patterns/">Patterns</a>: a catalog of integration patterns on one template.</li>
        <li><a href="/paths/">Paths</a>: learning sequences for connecting ServiceNow to the cloud and beyond.</li>
        <li><a href="/drift-log/">Drift Log</a>: my own learning journal, including what did not go to plan.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
      <p>
        Code and examples live on <a href={SITE.github}>GitHub</a>. [Add the contact method you want public.]
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
